const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文使用市场价格和基于会计的预期，构造隐含资本成本，而不是直接观察投资者要求回报。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article develops an implied cost-of-capital approach using market prices and accounting-based expectations rather than observing investors' required return directly. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它把估值输入与预期会计表现放入隐含回报框架，预测构造和时点是估计的一部分。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It connects valuation inputs and expected future accounting performance in an implied-return framework, so forecast construction and timing are integral to the estimate. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入包括时点价格、账面价值、收益或预测、分配假设、财年日期、证券身份、分析师信息可得性和估值期限。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Inputs include point-in-time price, book value, earnings or forecasts, payout assumptions, fiscal dates, security identity, analyst-information availability, and valuation horizon. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"隐含估计依赖模型与预测输入，不是观察到的融资利率或实现回报保证。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"An implied estimate is conditional on the model and forecast inputs; it is not an observed financing rate or a guarantee of realized return. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"只使用估计日可得信息；保留预测版本、拆股调整、货币、会计准则、缺失规则和精确估值设定。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Use information available at the estimation date; preserve forecast vintages, split adjustments, currency, accounting standards, missing-data rules, and the exact valuation specification. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Accounting Research (2001)。不同预测来源和估值假设会显著改变隐含估计，它不构成当前投资建议或普适贴现率。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Accounting Research (2001). Different forecast sources and valuation assumptions can materially change an implied estimate, so it is not a current investment recommendation or a universal discount rate. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1475-679x.00007",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (2001) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Toward an Implied Cost of Capital”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。不同预测来源和估值假设会显著改变隐含估计，它不构成当前投资建议或普适贴现率。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Toward an Implied Cost of Capital”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
